		{"id":"b899d8fd05e60755","type":"text","text":"[Tone]","x":-620,"y":-194,"width":250,"height":220},
		{"id":"e4ce0f2c27c7ebf7","type":"text","text":"[skills]\n\n1. **AI Literacy**: Understanding the basics of artificial intelligence, including how generative AI operates and can be applied in various nonprofit management contexts such as program development, fundraising, stewardship, and grant writing/reporting.\n    \n2. **Data Analysis and Interpretation**: Skills in analyzing and interpreting data to inform decision-making, especially in the context of donor research, program impact assessment, and identifying grant opportunities.\n    \n3. **Strategic Thinking and Planning**: Ability to use AI tools for strategic planning, including developing logic models for program development, creating targeted fundraising strategies, and planning personalized donor stewardship approaches.\n    \n4. **Creative Problem-Solving**: Leveraging AI for ideation and design, requiring creativity to solve problems and innovate within program development, fundraising campaigns, and donor engagement strategies.\n    \n5. **Technical Proficiency with AI Tools**: Competence in navigating and utilizing specific AI tools and platforms that assist in tasks such as donor segmentation, content creation for fundraising, and automated reporting.\n    \n6. **Communication and Persuasion**: Skills in crafting persuasive and engaging content with the help of AI, including writing grant proposals, fundraising appeals, and personalized donor communications.\n    \n7. **Project Management**: Managing projects effectively, from the ideation phase with AI through to execution, including organizing fundraising campaigns, overseeing program development, and handling grant reporting processes.\n    \n8. **Ethical Consideration and Bias Awareness**: Understanding the ethical implications of using AI in nonprofit management, including issues related to data privacy, donor consent, and being aware of and mitigating biases in AI-generated content and decision-making processes.\n","x":895,"y":-823,"width":810,"height":1783},
		{"id":"6b08fd22e19786b1","type":"text","text":"{{[[Course Builder V1/Project Creator]]}} create a project for {{outline}}","x":-3920,"y":4363,"width":250,"height":197,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e206a944b2d106de","type":"text","text":"### Module 3: Stewardship\n\n## 3.1 Rationale for Stewardship in Nonprofits\n- Understand the fundamental role of stewardship in maintaining and strengthening donor relationships.\n- Explore the impact of donor retention on the financial sustainability of nonprofits.\n- Relate the importance of stewardship to the broader goals of nonprofit effectiveness and trust-building.\n\n## 3.2 Expectations for AI-Enhanced Stewardship\n- Expect to develop the ability to use generative AI for crafting personalized communication with donors.\n- Be able to automate routine stewardship tasks, freeing up time for strategic engagement.\n- Acquire the skill to analyze donor feedback efficiently, leading to more effective stewardship strategies.\n\n## 3.3 Pre-Assessment of Stewardship Knowledge\n- Assess understanding of basic stewardship principles and why they matter.\n- Gauge familiarity with using technology in donor relations.\n- Identify current practices in donor stewardship and areas for improvement.\n\nMultiple Choice Example: \"What is the primary goal of donor stewardship in nonprofit organizations?\"\n- A) To secure one-time donations\n- B) To maintain and strengthen ongoing donor relationships\n- C) To reduce overall spending\n- D) To focus solely on high-net-worth individuals\n\n(Explanation: B is correct. This module will emphasize the importance of ongoing relationships, which you can learn more about in subtopic 3.4.)\n\n## 3.4 Concepts and Theories in Stewardship and AI\n- Define donor stewardship and its key components.\n- Introduce generative AI and its relevance to nonprofits.\n- Explain how AI can be used to enhance personalized communication and donor engagement.\n\n## 3.5 Walkthrough of Generative AI Tools for Stewardship\n- Step-by-step guidance on using AI tools to segment donor data for personalized outreach.\n- Detailed instructions on setting up automated thank-you messages and feedback surveys.\n- Demonstrate how to generate impact reports using AI to illustrate donation outcomes.\n\n## 3.6 Best Practices in AI-Enhanced Donor Stewardship\n- Discuss the importance of personalization in donor communications and how AI can help achieve it.\n- Outline the best practices for setting up and maintaining an automated stewardship system.\n- Share effective approaches to using AI for donor engagement while maintaining a personal touch.\n\n## 3.7 Case Study: Implementing AI in Donor Stewardship\n- Create a scenario involving a nonprofit organization's transition to AI-enhanced stewardship.\n- Illustrate the step-by-step process of selecting and implementing generative AI tools.\n- Share the outcomes, challenges, and lessons learned from AI integration in donor relations.\n\n## 3.8 Application of Skills in Stewardship Using Generative AI\n- Provide a simulated task where learners craft a personalized donor communication strategy using AI.\n- Set up an interactive exercise to create and automate a donor feedback collection process.\n- Engage learners in developing a visually appealing impact report using AI-generated content and data analysis.\n\nWith the completion of Module 3, learners will be equipped with practical, hands-on skills for leveraging generative AI in the stewardship and donor relations aspect of nonprofit management, ensuring they are job-ready in this evolving technological landscape.","x":120,"y":1880,"width":1640,"height":1600,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"6d4cb37e40c281eb","type":"text","text":"[audience]\n","x":-340,"y":-194,"width":250,"height":220},
		{"id":"18795c84f0d61402","type":"text","text":"## 3.1 Rationale for Stewardship in Nonprofits\n\nIn the realm of nonprofit management, the concepts of stewardship and donor relations are not mere niceties; they are essential strategies for survival and growth. Stewardship is the careful and responsible management of something entrusted to one's care. For nonprofits, this means not only managing funds and resources efficiently but also nurturing relationships with those who provide these assets: the donors.\n\n**Why is this critical?** Well, consider this: a robust stewardship program can transform one-time givers into lifelong supporters, thereby securing a steady stream of resources necessary for the organization's operations and initiatives. It's about more than just saying \"thank you.\" Effective stewardship fosters deep connections, engenders trust, and demonstrates impact, which in turn can lead to increased donor engagement and investment.\n\nMoreover, donor retention is significantly more cost-effective than donor acquisition. It's well documented that keeping an existing donor is less resource-intensive than finding a new one. By focusing on stewardship, nonprofits can create a sustainable fundraising model that supports long-term success.\n\nIn this module, you will uncover how stewardship is intertwined with the overarching objectives of nonprofit efficacy, accountability, and reputation. It's about creating a virtuous cycle where good stewardship leads to loyal donors, which leads to stronger impact, and back around again. Recognizing the gravity of stewardship is the first step in leveraging it to its full potential.","x":-2600,"y":1880,"width":888,"height":1147,"color":"6"},
